        key "gQInj3H6"
        doc "TODO"
    }

    field base_hp type="u32::str" {
        key "e7DK0FQT"
        doc """
        Current HP stat for this unit before imp/stat-up bonuses.
        Includes level-based stat growth because this client passes
        base_hp into GameUtils::getUnitHp(base_hp, unit_lvl, ...),
        which currently returns base_hp unchanged. This suggests the
        server is expected to store the unit's level-adjusted normal
        HP in this bucket. Naturally, this applies to all base_* stats.
        """
    }

    field add_hp type="i32::str" {
        key "cuIWp89g"
        doc """
        A stat bonus that folds SILENTLY into the displayed total.
        setAddHp, vtable-dispatched from readParam.

        ⚠ NOT THE IMP BUCKET -- that is ext_hp.  Probed in-client
        2026-09-05 with distinct values in both buckets on one unit:
        the card drew "HP 5365 [111]" from base 5243 + add 11 +
        ext 111, so the big stat is base+add+ext and the small orange
        figure beside it is ext_* ALONE.

        // UNVERIFIED: what actually feeds this.  Nothing on this
        server writes it, and nothing should until its source is known.
        """
    }

    field ext_hp type="u32::str" {
        key "TokWs1B3"
        doc """
        THE IMP BUCKET, and the small orange number the unit card draws
        beside the HP stat.  CONFIRMED in-client 2026-09-05 by probing
        add_* and ext_* with distinct values: the card showed
        "HP 5365 [111]" for base 5243 + add 11 + ext 111.

        Written by UnitMix, clamped to UnitMst.param_max (imQJdg64) for
        this stat -- the cap the orange figure is measured against.
